---
import BlogPost from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

// Figures match each burger's item page.
const burgers = [
  { name: 'FlameThrower Stackburger', href: '/items/flamethrower-stackburger', price: '$10.87', cal: '720', note: 'Spicy: jalapeño bacon, pepper jack and FlameThrower sauce' },
  { name: 'Backyard Bacon Ranch Stackburger', href: '/items/backyard-bacon-ranch-stackburger', price: '$9.99', cal: '820', note: 'Bacon, ranch, BBQ sauce and crispy onions' },
  { name: 'Two Cheese Deluxe Stackburger', href: '/items/two-cheese-deluxe-stackburger', price: '$8.29', cal: '620', note: 'Two patties, cheese, pickles, onion, ketchup and mustard' },
  { name: 'Mushroom Swiss Stackburger', href: '/items/mushroom-swiss-stackburger', price: '$9.49', cal: '680', note: 'Grilled mushrooms and Swiss cheese' },
  { name: 'Double Cheeseburger', href: '/items/double-cheeseburger', price: '$7.99', cal: '570', note: 'Classic and simple, the best value pick' },
  { name: 'Original Cheeseburger', href: '/items/original-cheeseburger', price: '$6.39', cal: '370', note: 'Lightest burger; also part of the $7 Meal Deal' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is the best burger at Dairy Queen?', a: 'The FlameThrower Stackburger is our top pick if you like heat. If you do not, the Backyard Bacon Ranch Stackburger is the best non-spicy burger. For value, the Double Cheeseburger is hard to beat.' },
  { q: 'What is a Stackburger?', a: 'Stackburger is Dairy Queen’s name for its signature burger line: seasoned beef patties with toppings such as bacon, ranch, mushrooms or spicy sauce on a toasted bun. They are sold at DQ Grill & Chill locations.' },
  { q: 'Is the FlameThrower burger spicy?', a: 'Yes, but most people find it a medium heat. The spice comes from FlameThrower sauce, jalapeño bacon and pepper jack cheese.' },
  { q: 'What is the cheapest burger at Dairy Queen?', a: 'The Original Cheeseburger is the lowest-priced burger, typically around $6.39 on its own. It is also one of the entrée choices in the $7 Meal Deal, which adds fries, a drink and a sundae.' },
];
---
<BlogPost
  title="Best Dairy Queen Burgers Ranked (2026)"
  description="The best burgers at Dairy Queen, ranked: FlameThrower, Bacon Ranch and other Stackburgers compared by taste, price and calories."
  h1="Best Dairy Queen Burgers, Ranked"
  crumb="Best DQ Burgers"
  eyebrow="Burger rankings · Stackburgers and classics"
  image="/Images/flamethrower-stackburger.webp"
  imageAlt="Dairy Queen FlameThrower Stackburger with pepper jack cheese and jalapeño bacon"
  datePublished="2026-06-01"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p class="lead"><strong>The best burger at Dairy Queen is the FlameThrower Stackburger</strong> if you like some heat, and the Backyard Bacon Ranch Stackburger if you do not. For the lowest price, the Double Cheeseburger gives you the most burger for the money. Here is how every DQ burger stacks up, with typical prices and calories.</p>

  <p>Dairy Queen is better known for Blizzards, but the burgers at DQ Grill &amp; Chill stores are better than many people expect. The patties are cooked on a flat-top grill, so they get a proper browned edge. Treat-only DQ locations do not sell burgers.</p>

  <h2 id="ranking">DQ burgers ranked</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Burger</th><th>Typical price</th><th>Calories</th><th>What’s on it</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {burgers.map((b, i) => (
          <tr>
            <td><strong>{i + 1}</strong></td>
            <td><strong><a href={b.href}>{b.name}</a></strong></td>
            <td class="price-cell">{b.price}</td>
            <td>{b.cal}</td>
            <td>{b.note}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="flamethrower">1. FlameThrower Stackburger: best overall</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/items/flamethrower-stackburger">FlameThrower</a> is the burger people come back for. It has spicy FlameThrower sauce, jalapeño bacon and pepper jack cheese, so the heat comes in layers instead of one hot sauce. It is warm, not painful. The Double has about 720 calories; the Triple is about 910, so the Double is enough for most people.</p>

  <h2 id="bacon-ranch">2. Backyard Bacon Ranch: best if you do not want spice</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/items/backyard-bacon-ranch-stackburger">Backyard Bacon Ranch</a> mixes smoky BBQ sauce with cool ranch, bacon and crispy onions. It is messy and very good. If you usually order a bacon cheeseburger somewhere else, order this.</p>

  <h2 id="two-cheese">3. Two Cheese Deluxe: the classic choice</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/items/two-cheese-deluxe-stackburger">Two Cheese Deluxe</a> is a straightforward double cheeseburger with pickles, onion, ketchup and mustard. It is the safest pick for picky eaters and a bit cheaper than the other Stackburgers.</p>

  <h2 id="mushroom-swiss">4. Mushroom Swiss: good, but not for everyone</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/items/mushroom-swiss-stackburger">Mushroom Swiss</a> is savory and filling. If you like mushroom burgers, you will like it. It just does not stand out as much as the top three.</p>

  <h2 id="value">Best value: Double Cheeseburger and the $7 Meal Deal</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/items/double-cheeseburger">Double Cheeseburger</a> is the best price-to-size option on the menu. If you want a full meal, the <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a> with the <a href="/items/original-cheeseburger">Original Cheeseburger</a> adds fries, a drink and a small sundae. Our <a href="/blog/dq-meal-deals-guide">DQ meal deals guide</a> compares every value option.</p>

  <h2 id="ordering-tips">Tips for ordering a burger at DQ</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can ask for no sauce, extra pickles or no onions; Stackburgers are made to order.</li>
    <li>Add a side of <a href="/items/cheese-curds">cheese curds</a> instead of fries if you want something different.</li>
    <li>Not a beef fan? The <a href="/items/crispy-chicken-sandwich">Crispy Chicken Sandwich</a> is the best non-burger sandwich.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>See every burger, sandwich and price on our <a href="/categories/burgers-sandwiches">Dairy Queen burgers menu</a>.</p>
</BlogPost>
